21
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,193
Claude never guesses a path.

22
00:00:55,193 --> 00:00:56,764
If a hop did not answer,

23
00:00:56,764 --> 00:00:58,074
the diagram says so.

24
00:00:58,824 --> 00:01:02,304
You begin with what traceroute and ping can actually

25
00:01:02,304 --> 00:01:04,178
prove, and what they cannot.

26
00:01:04,178 --> 00:01:08,394
Asymmetric return paths. Load balancers that hide pool members.

27
00:01:08,394 --> 00:01:10,268
Firewalls that drop I C M P.

28
00:01:10,268 --> 00:01:12,276
Then you set up the workbench.

29
00:01:12,276 --> 00:01:14,150
Claude Code on your machine,

30
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:16,358
the Claude Agent S D K in Python,

31
00:01:16,358 --> 00:01:18,834
and an M C P server that exposes only

32
00:01:18,834 --> 00:01:22,114
read only probe tools, with every call logged and

33
00:01:22,114 --> 00:01:24,456
credentials kept out of the prompt.

34
00:01:25,206 --> 00:01:27,419
Next you build the probe runners.

35
00:01:27,419 --> 00:01:31,241
Deterministic Python wrappers around ping and traceroute,

36
00:01:31,241 --> 00:01:34,929
with timeouts, retries and parsers that turn raw output

37
00:01:34,929 --> 00:01:36,606
